  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA value remains network-concentrated:</strong> the top chains continue to capture the majority of distributed issuance and often set near-term market direction. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/09/14/sec-s-atkins-backs-clarity-act-but-says-agency-will-keep-pushing-crypto-rules-without-it\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SEC&#x27;s Atkins backs Clarity Act but says agency will keep pushing crypto rules without it</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Institutional expansion is likely staged:</strong> large-scale adoption typically lands on proven networks first, then broadens as compliance, interoperability, and liquidity deepen. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/people/kamino-names-michael-weisz-ceo-for-us-and-institutional-expansion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Kamino Names Michael Weisz CEO for US and Institutional Expansion</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Custody and issuance integrations are moving rankings first:</strong> Chains that win custody and issuance integrations usually pull distributed value share before the broader RWA market total catches up. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/defi/2026-09-15-zama-expands-confidential-morpho-lineup-after-first-vault-hits-40-million-launches-private-swaps-on-ethereum-414613\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Zama expands confidential Morpho lineup after first vault hits $40 million, launches private swaps on Ethereum</a> (The Block).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
